From: Misectel <support@misectel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fstools: notify factoryreset hooks before removing the overlay

Allow platform services to prepare for reset while their programs and
configuration are still available. This also covers -r, which calls reboot(2)
directly instead of going through procd's shutdown hooks.

--- a/factoryreset.c
+++ b/factoryreset.c
@@ -47,6 +47,11 @@ static int jffs2_reset(struct volume *v, int reset, int keep)
 {
 	char *mp;
 
+	if (!access("/sbin/hotplug-call", X_OK) &&
+	    system("ACTION=reset /sbin/hotplug-call factoryreset"))
+		ULOG_WARN("factoryreset preparation hook failed\n");
+
+	/* Notify before overlay_delete removes hook programs and configuration. */
 	mp = find_mount_point(v->blk, 1);
 	if (mp) {
 		ULOG_INFO("%s is mounted as %s, only erasing files\n", v->blk, mp);
